    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration limit in the owner creation endpoint.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 after the existing duplicate/conflict checks, it now rejects with **400 Bad Request** when the daily limit is reached:\n\n```java\nif (dailyRegistrationLimitReached()) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\n```\n\nThe new helper counts stored owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and returns `true` once 20 exist:\n\n```java\nprivate static final long MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 20;\n\nprivate boolean dailyRegistrationLimitReached() {\n    LocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\n    long registeredToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n        .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))\n        .count();\n    return registeredToday >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY;\n}\n```\n\nThis is the only endpoint that creates owners (the V2 controller is read-only). Since new owners default their `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when unset, the 20th creation succeeds and the 21st for the day is rejected. Seed owners carry no registration date, so they never count toward the limit.\n\n**Test added** \u2014 `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` seeds 20 owners registered today and asserts the next POST returns 400.",
